# Frontend rules

- Match the design: `design/png/<Board>.png` for the look, `design/boards/<Board>.dc.html` for exact copy, spacing and
  colours. The blue and yellow bars at the top of boards are design annotations, not product UI.
- Use the shared components in `web/src/components` (Components and States boards). Don't restyle shared patterns
  per page. Colours and type only from `web/src/styles/tokens.css`. Both are created in M1 (story M1-FE-01,
  layout in `docs/specs/frontend/README.md`); until then M0 uses `web/src/styles.css`.
- API types come from `npm run gen:api` (openapi-typescript over `docs/specs/contracts/openapi.yaml`); never
  hand-write request or response types.
- The screens are platform screens; procurement content on the boards is example data. Nothing in `web/src` is
  named after or written for one pack: stage names come from `snapshot.stages`, document tabs from
  `ArtifactSummary.view` (type, columns, field labels), workflows from `listDigitalWorkers`. Use the board's layout,
  not its example strings.
- Render kernel state; never compute permissions, hide columns or infer state in the browser. Disabled controls show
  the reason the payload gives.
- Pages: load the snapshot, then follow the event stream from its cursor; on `snapshot.required` reload. Apply events
  in `id` order and ignore duplicates.
- Agent content renders from typed blocks only. Never `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`, never render Markdown from the model.
- Writes send `expected_version` / `payload_hash` / `base_version`; a 409 shows `ConflictNotice` and reloads.
- Problem → component mapping is in `docs/specs/frontend/README.md`; use it, don't invent error UI.
- Accessible: real buttons and links, labels, focus states, 44 px targets in the Workspace; works at phone width.
